From accb157d9f283fda9697fbdc98580448cec2f77a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: DoubleGate <parobek@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 25 Nov 2026 23:11:33 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] [UPSTREAM] notifications: optional Authorization header for
 ntfy

Add an optional `ntfy_auth` config value sent as the `Authorization` header
on each ntfy request, for a protected ntfy topic or a reverse-proxied
endpoint (e.g. "Bearer tk_..." or "Basic <base64>"). Unset by default, so
nothing changes for an unauthenticated endpoint.

`ntfy_auth` is a secret: it is redacted from `GET /api/config` (like
`wifi_password`). Because the config API is unauthenticated, the stored
secret is preserved across a config write that omits it ONLY when `ntfy_url`
is unchanged -- a write that repoints `ntfy_url` drops the stored credential
so it cannot be smuggled to a new endpoint, and it must be re-supplied. An
explicit empty string clears it. This resolution is a pure, unit-tested
helper (resolve_ntfy_auth) covering preserve / drop-on-url-change / clear /
replace.

The `/api/test-notification` endpoint also sends the configured `Authorization`
header, so the web UI Test button (and `orx alert test`) reaches a protected
endpoint just like a real notification.

Ref: Orbic-Rayhunter T-OR-046.
Signed-off-by: DoubleGate <parobek@gmail.com>
